<title>USA: Maine Gov. seen announcing Sears Island plans soon.</title>
<headline>Maine Gov. seen announcing Sears Island plans soon.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine Gov. Angus King was expected to announce Monday his plans to buy Sears Island.</p>
<p>The option to buy the island runs out today.</p>
<p>King convinced lawmakers to put $2 million in the state budget for the purchase, but the cash will not be available until July.</p>
<p>The governor has been working behind the scenes to get an extension on the option.</p>
<p>Several groups opposing developing a cargo port on the island are worried that King plans to move forward to do that without considering other uses of the Penobscot Bay island.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
